From: canoziia <canoziia@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] router: abort backend requests when the client disconnects

Ported from vllm-project/production-stack PR #1040 (open, "[Router][Bugfix]
propagate client cancellation", fixes issue #634): route_general_request
races the backend reply against the ASGI http.disconnect message (same as
vllm.entrypoints.utils.with_cancellation, no is_disconnected() polling) and
cancels the pending call, which closes the backend connection; X-Request-Id
is CR/LF-stripped before logging. The PR's on_request_complete-in-finally
hunks are already in vllm-stack-0.1.13 and are not taken.

Extended to the PD path (route_disaggregated_prefill_request), which the PR
does not cover: the prefill hop and the non-streaming decode hop are raced
against http.disconnect the same way; on disconnect the hop is cancelled,
its aiohttp response is closed (never returned to the pool), a warning with
request id, phase and waited seconds is logged, and 499 is returned. The
streaming decode hop is already cancelled by Starlette (ASGI spec 2.3) on
disconnect; send_request_to_decode now closes the socket explicitly and the
disconnect is logged. Without a disconnect nothing changes.
